#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:153
msgid "Usage"
msgstr "用法"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:163
msgid ""
"Reach for this command to profile a **real, unmodified process** (a "
"production or vLLM-driven server under actual traffic, an idle server, or"
" any arbitrary PID) without standing up a benchmark harness. The "
"``bench`` commands (``lmcache bench l2`` / ``lmcache bench server``) "
"instead profile a process under synthetic load they generate."
msgstr "使用此命令可以对 **真实的、未修改的进程**（在实际流量下的生产或 vLLM 驱动的服务器、空闲服务器或任何任意 PID）进行性能分析，而无需搭建基准测试工具。``bench`` 命令（``lmcache bench l2`` / ``lmcache bench server``）则是在它们生成的合成负载下对进程进行性能分析。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:170
msgid "Modes"
msgstr "模式"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:174
msgid ""
"LMCache is mostly Python, so the first question is usually where Python "
"time goes and how contended the GIL is. **To profile Python execution or "
"GIL contention**, use ``gil`` / ``wall`` (``py-spy``): one root frame per"
" thread, attaching to an **unmodified** CPython target, but with no "
"kernel frames."
msgstr "LMCache 主要是用 Python 编写的，因此第一个问题通常是 Python 时间的去向以及 GIL 的争用情况。**要分析 Python 执行或 GIL 争用情况**，请使用 ``gil`` / ``wall`` (``py-spy``)：每个线程一个根帧，附加到 **未修改的** CPython 目标，但没有内核帧。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:179
msgid ""
"**gil**: only threads holding the GIL, so interpreter-lock contention is "
"directly visible (the default for a live server)."
msgstr "**gil**：仅显示持有 GIL 的线程，因此解释器锁的争用直接可见（这是实时服务器的默认设置）。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:181
msgid "**wall**: wall-clock time per thread, blocked threads included."
msgstr "**墙**：每个线程的墙钟时间，包括被阻塞的线程。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:183
msgid ""
"But LMCache also uses C++, Rust, and CUDA to accelerate hot paths and "
"release the GIL, and py-spy sees none of that. **To profile CPU/IO time, "
"kernel frames, context switches, or a non-Python process** (or to get a "
"cross-language picture of where the whole process spends time and "
"blocks), use the whole-process modes (``perf`` / bcc): every thread, "
"kernel frames, scheduler activity, any process, but merged into one "
"chart."
msgstr "但是 LMCache 还使用 C++、Rust 和 CUDA 来加速热路径并释放 GIL，而 py-spy 并未看到这些。**要分析 CPU/IO 时间、内核帧、上下文切换或非 Python 进程**（或获取整个进程花费时间和阻塞的跨语言视图），请使用整个进程模式（``perf`` / bcc）：每个线程、内核帧、调度器活动、任何进程，但合并为一个图表。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:190
msgid "**on-cpu** (``perf``): where CPU *cycles* go."
msgstr "**在 CPU 上** (``perf``): CPU *周期* 的去向。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:191
msgid "**off-cpu** (``offcputime-bpfcc``): time spent *blocked* (I/O, locks)."
msgstr "**离线 CPU** (``offcputime-bpfcc``): 花费在 *阻塞* 上的时间（I/O，锁）。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:192
msgid ""
"**wakeup** (``wakeuptime-bpfcc``): the stacks that *do* the waking, "
"ending others' sleep."
msgstr "**唤醒** (``wakeuptime-bpfcc``): *唤醒* 的堆栈，结束其他线程的睡眠。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:194
msgid ""
"**offwake** (``offwaketime-bpfcc``): ``off-cpu`` and ``wakeup`` combined,"
" each blocked stack joined to the stack of the thread that woke it (that "
"waker half drawn inverted on top). Use it when ``off-cpu`` shows a big "
"blocked tower and you need the cause."
msgstr "**offwake** (``offwaketime-bpfcc``): ``off-cpu`` 和 ``wakeup`` 的结合，每个被阻塞的栈与唤醒它的线程的栈相连（唤醒者的部分反向绘制在顶部）。当 ``off-cpu`` 显示出一个大的阻塞塔时使用它，以便找出原因。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:199
msgid ""
"**How they work.** All run as external processes; what differs is *where "
"the data is collected*, in the kernel (perf, bcc) or by reading the "
"target's memory (py-spy):"
msgstr "**它们是如何工作的。** 所有运行作为外部进程；不同之处在于 *数据的收集位置*，是在内核中（perf, bcc）还是通过读取目标的内存（py-spy）："

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:203
msgid ""
"**perf** samples the CPU at 99 Hz, recording the running thread's stack, "
"so it sees only on-CPU work and walks native stacks via frame pointers."
msgstr "**perf** 以 99 Hz 的频率对 CPU 进行采样，记录正在运行的线程的调用栈，因此它只看到 CPU 上的工作，并通过帧指针遍历本地调用栈。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:205
msgid ""
"**bcc** is *not* sampled: an eBPF program fires on scheduler events, so "
"it can measure *blocked* time perf cannot, at a cost that grows with the "
"target's context-switch rate. Loading eBPF needs privilege."
msgstr "**bcc** *不是* 被采样的：eBPF 程序在调度事件上触发，因此它可以测量 perf 无法测量的 *阻塞* 时间，代价随着目标的上下文切换率而增加。加载 eBPF 需要特权。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:208
msgid ""
"**py-spy** works in user space, reading the target's memory "
"(``process_vm_readv``) with ``--nonblocking`` (no pause); it sees only "
"Python frames and needs ``ptrace`` permission."
msgstr "**py-spy** 在用户空间工作，通过 ``process_vm_readv`` 读取目标的内存，并使用 ``--nonblocking``（无暂停）；它只看到 Python 框架，并需要 ``ptrace`` 权限。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:212
msgid "**Equivalent raw commands** for ``--pid P``:"
msgstr "**``--pid P`` 的等效原始命令：**"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:223
msgid ""
"**Native stacks need frame pointers.** The perf/bcc modes unwind native "
"stacks through frame pointers (perf via ``-g``, bcc via "
"``bpf_get_stackid``), so a target built with ``-fomit-frame-pointer`` "
"shows broken C stacks in either; rebuild with ``-fno-omit-frame-"
"pointer``. py-spy is unaffected (it reads the interpreter) but sees only "
"Python."
msgstr "**本地堆栈需要帧指针。** perf/bcc 模式通过帧指针展开本地堆栈（perf 通过 ``-g``，bcc 通过 ``bpf_get_stackid``），因此使用 ``-fomit-frame-pointer`` 构建的目标在两者中都会显示损坏的 C 堆栈；请使用 ``-fno-omit-frame-pointer`` 重新构建。py-spy 不受影响（它读取解释器），但仅看到 Python。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:231
msgid "Installation"
msgstr "安装"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:233
msgid ""
"Each mode wraps an external tool that must be installed on the host "
"running the command (the same host as the target); a missing one fails "
"fast naming what to install."
msgstr "每种模式都封装了一个必须在运行命令的主机上安装的外部工具（与目标相同的主机）；缺少工具时会快速失败并指明需要安装的内容。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:237
msgid ""
"`py-spy <https://github.com/benfred/py-spy>`__ (``wall`` / ``gil``): "
"reads the interpreter and renders its own SVG. Install with ``pip install"
" py-spy``."
msgstr "`py-spy <https://github.com/benfred/py-spy>`__ (``wall`` / ``gil``): 读取解释器并渲染自己的 SVG。使用 ``pip install py-spy`` 安装。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:240
msgid ""
"Linux ``perf`` (``on-cpu``): ``sudo apt install linux-tools-generic`` "
"(Debian / Ubuntu) or ``sudo dnf install perf`` (Fedora / RHEL); the "
"package must match the running kernel. Rendered with the FlameGraph "
"scripts below."
msgstr "Linux ``perf`` (``on-cpu``): ``sudo apt install linux-tools-generic`` (Debian / Ubuntu) 或 ``sudo dnf install perf`` (Fedora / RHEL)；该软件包必须与正在运行的内核匹配。使用下面的 FlameGraph 脚本进行渲染。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:243
msgid ""
"`bcc <https://github.com/iovisor/bcc>`__ (``off-cpu`` / ``wakeup`` / "
"``offwake``): ``sudo apt install bpfcc-tools`` (Debian / Ubuntu) or "
"``sudo dnf install bcc-tools`` (Fedora / RHEL). Its ``*-bpfcc`` tools "
"also need ``sudo`` at run time."
msgstr "`bcc <https://github.com/iovisor/bcc>`__ (``off-cpu`` / ``wakeup`` / ``offwake``): ``sudo apt install bpfcc-tools`` (Debian / Ubuntu) 或 ``sudo dnf install bcc-tools`` (Fedora / RHEL)。其 ``*-bpfcc`` 工具在运行时也需要 ``sudo``。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:247
msgid ""
"`FlameGraph <https://github.com/brendangregg/FlameGraph>`__, by Brendan "
"Gregg: folds and renders the perf/bcc SVGs. Cloned to ``~/FlameGraph`` on"
" first use (needs ``git``); or point ``--flamegraph-scripts-dir`` at an "
"existing checkout."
msgstr "`FlameGraph <https://github.com/brendangregg/FlameGraph>`__，由 Brendan Gregg 提供：折叠并渲染 perf/bcc SVG。首次使用时克隆到 ``~/FlameGraph``（需要 ``git``）；或者将 ``--flamegraph-scripts-dir`` 指向现有的检出版本。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:253
msgid "Permissions"
msgstr "权限"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:255
msgid ""
"**Naming Python frames in the perf/bcc modes** requires the target to "
"have been *started* with ``PYTHONPERFSUPPORT=1`` (its perf trampoline "
"map); you cannot enable it on a running process."
msgstr "**在 perf/bcc 模式中命名 Python 框架** 需要目标在启动时设置 ``PYTHONPERFSUPPORT=1``（其 perf 跳板图）；您无法在运行中的进程上启用它。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:261
msgid ""
"**If it was not set:** perf/bcc still record, but Python frames collapse "
"to ``[unknown]`` (C/native stack only). Use ``gil`` / ``wall``, or "
"restart the target with the variable set."
msgstr "**如果未设置：** perf/bcc 仍然会记录，但 Python 框架会合并为 ``[unknown]``（仅 C/本地堆栈）。使用 ``gil`` / ``wall``，或在设置变量的情况下重新启动目标。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:264
msgid ""
"**If it is set:** it adds a standing per-call overhead for the process's "
"lifetime, so reserve it for a dedicated profiling session, not "
"production."
msgstr "**如果设置了：** 这会在进程的生命周期内增加每次调用的固定开销，因此请将其保留用于专门的性能分析会话，而不是生产环境。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:268
msgid ""
"**System settings to adjust (bare-metal / VM).** Each tool needs a kernel"
" permission; set the one for your mode, or run as root, which satisfies "
"all three:"
msgstr "**系统设置调整（裸机 / 虚拟机）。** 每个工具需要内核权限；设置适合您模式的权限，或者以 root 身份运行，这样可以满足所有三种情况："

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:272
msgid ""
"``wall`` / ``gil`` (py-spy) read the target's memory via ``ptrace``, "
"gated by Yama. Ubuntu / Debian default ``ptrace_scope`` to ``1`` (trace "
"only descendants), which blocks attaching to a server:"
msgstr "``wall`` / ``gil`` (py-spy) 通过 ``ptrace`` 读取目标的内存，受 Yama 限制。Ubuntu / Debian 默认将 ``ptrace_scope`` 设置为 ``1``（仅跟踪子进程），这会阻止附加到服务器："

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:280
msgid ""
"``CAP_SYS_PTRACE`` (or root) bypasses it; py-spy also prints this hint "
"when it is blocked."
msgstr "``CAP_SYS_PTRACE``（或 root）可以绕过它；当被阻止时，py-spy 也会打印此提示。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:282
msgid ""
"``on-cpu`` (perf) samples via ``perf_event_open``. Level ``3`` (a Debian "
"addition) blocks it outright, and any level above ``2`` makes ``perf "
"record`` silently write an empty file, so lower it:"
msgstr "``on-cpu`` (perf) 通过 ``perf_event_open`` 进行采样。级别 ``3``（Debian 的附加功能）会直接阻止它，任何高于 ``2`` 的级别会使 ``perf record`` 静默写入一个空文件，因此请降低它："

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:290
msgid ""
"``off-cpu`` / ``wakeup`` / ``offwake`` (bcc) load an eBPF program, so "
"their ``*-bpfcc`` tools need ``sudo`` (root)."
msgstr "``off-cpu`` / ``wakeup`` / ``offwake`` (bcc) 加载一个 eBPF 程序，因此它们的 ``*-bpfcc`` 工具需要 ``sudo``（root 权限）。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:295
msgid ""
"**In a container, use the py-spy modes.** perf and bcc gate on host-wide "
"kernel state a container should not change, so run them on the host (the "
"settings above apply there)."
msgstr "**在容器中，使用 py-spy 模式。** perf 和 bcc 依赖于主机范围的内核状态，容器不应更改，因此在主机上运行它们（上述设置适用于此）。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:299
msgid ""
"py-spy works inside a container. Run the profiler in the **same "
"container** as the target (or share its PID namespace with "
"``--pid=container:<target>``) and start the container with ``--cap-add "
"SYS_PTRACE``, the container equivalent of the ``ptrace_scope`` setting "
"above:"
msgstr "py-spy 可以在容器内工作。请在与目标 **相同的容器** 中运行分析器（或使用 ``--pid=container:<target>`` 共享其 PID 命名空间），并使用 ``--cap-add SYS_PTRACE`` 启动容器，这是上述 ``ptrace_scope`` 设置的容器等效项："

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:310
msgid ""
"If the platform will not grant ``CAP_SYS_PTRACE`` (RunPod, some "
"Kubernetes), you can still profile a process you start yourself: tracing "
"your own child needs no capability, so launch the target **under** py-spy"
" instead of attaching to it:"
msgstr "如果平台不授予 ``CAP_SYS_PTRACE``（如 RunPod、某些 Kubernetes），您仍然可以对自己启动的进程进行分析：跟踪您自己的子进程不需要任何权限，因此请在 py-spy 下启动目标，而不是附加到它上。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:323
msgid "Cost"
msgstr "成本"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:325
msgid "The mechanisms give each mode a different cost *shape*:"
msgstr "这些机制为每种模式提供了不同的成本 *形状*："

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:327
msgid ""
"**perf**: *bounded*, a fixed 99 Hz sample, so overhead is constant; the "
"cost is disk, as ``perf.data`` grows with duration × rate × threads × "
"depth (deleted once rendered)."
msgstr "**perf**: *有界*，固定的 99 Hz 采样，因此开销是恒定的；成本是磁盘，因为 ``perf.data`` 随着持续时间 × 速率 × 线程 × 深度而增长（渲染后删除）。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:330
msgid ""
"**bcc**: *unbounded*, firing on every scheduler event ties cost to the "
"target's event rate, so a busy service fires the probe constantly. Output"
" is tiny."
msgstr "**bcc**: *无界*，在每个调度程序事件上触发，成本与目标的事件速率相关，因此繁忙的服务会不断触发探针。输出非常小。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:333
msgid ""
"**py-spy**: lightest *on the target*, its sampling runs off the target's "
"CPUs, whereas perf and bcc steal the target's cycles."
msgstr "**py-spy**: 最轻量级的 *在目标上*，其采样运行在目标的 CPU 上，而 perf 和 bcc 则占用目标的周期。"

#: ../../source/cli/tool.rst:336
msgid ""
"On a production server, prefer ``wall`` / ``gil`` and keep ``--duration``"
" short; if you need a whole-process mode, ``on-cpu``'s bounded cost is "
"safer than the bcc modes on a busy target."
msgstr "在生产服务器上，优先使用 ``wall`` / ``gil`` 并保持 ``--duration`` 较短；如果需要整个进程模式，``on-cpu`` 的有限成本比在繁忙目标上的 bcc 模式更安全。"

